All Day 9 checks passed.
All Day 9 checks pass end-to-end, and this also fixed the response_format bug that would have affected Day 8 agents too. Here's what was built:

Day 9 — 5 files created:

mcp_platform/mcp/tools/search_similar_interventions.py — MCP Tool 1. Lazy-loads Embedder (PyTorch) and InterventionsCollection (ChromaDB) on first call. Embeds the issue text, runs semantic search against ats_interventions, returns list[CaseStudy]. Returns [] gracefully if ChromaDB is down.

mcp_platform/mcp/tools/fetch_best_practices.py — MCP Tool 2. Looks up best-practice entries by issue_type tag. Critically, has a built-in fallback table (4 entries covering slow_assessment, high_rejection, offer_decline, sourcing_quality) so the agent always returns useful steps even without ChromaDB. Issue text is normalised to canonical type via keyword matching.

mcp_platform/mcp/mcp_client.py — Thin facade with asyncio.wait_for timeout (default 10 s from settings). fetch_evidence() calls both tools concurrently via asyncio.gather.

agents/insight/improvement_action/rejection_analyser.py — Pure Python. Groups rejection records by rejection_category/reason into canonical issue_type buckets, counts per stage, assigns severity (high ≥ 25%, medium ≥ 10%), returns RejectionReport with to_text() for the LLM prompt.

agents/insight/improvement_action/improvement_action_agent.py — ImprovementActionAgent(BaseAgent). Calls detect_top_issues(), then fans out mcp.fetch_evidence() concurrently for each high/medium issue, assembles MCP evidence into the data summary, calls _call_llm().

Bug fixed: response_format was incorrectly nested in model_kwargs in llm_client.py — fixed to pass it as a top-level bind kwarg. This fix applies to all agents (Day 8 and 9).

Next is Day 10: ResourceOptimization, OfferInsights, Evaluation, and Optimization agents.

