PowerShell

$body = @'
{
  "query": "Why is our hiring process slow and where are candidates dropping off?",
  "scenario": "fix_slow_hiring",
  "filters": { "department": "Engineering" },
  "max_agents": 5
}
'@

Invoke-RestMethod -Uri http://localhost:8080/api/v1/analysis/run `
  -Method Post `
  -Body $body `
  -ContentType "application/json" | ConvertTo-Json -Depth 6
What the fields mean
Field	Required	What to put
query	Yes	Any hiring question in plain English
scenario	No	One of the 5 named scenarios — locks the agent set. Omit for free-form routing
filters	No	Optional department, location, etc. passed to all agents
max_agents	No	Default 5 — leave as-is
Other queries to try
Free-form (no scenario — RoutingAgent decides which agents to call):


{
  "query": "Which sourcing channels are bringing in the best candidates?",
  "filters": {}
}
Investigate rejections:


{
  "query": "Why are so many candidates being rejected at the technical interview stage?",
  "scenario": "investigate_rejections",
  "filters": {}
}
Full executive report:


{
  "query": "Give me a complete hiring health report.",
  "scenario": "executive_metrics",
  "filters": {}
}
Note: The /run endpoint works without structured_data — agents will still run but their metrics will show zero/empty data since no DB records are passed in. To get meaningful numbers, use POST /api/v1/analysis/scenario/{name} which accepts a structured_data body. Want a sample for that too?

{
  "query": "string",
  "scenario": "string",
  "filters": {
    "additionalProp1": {}
  },
  "max_agents": 5
}
That's the Swagger default placeholder — replace it with this and hit Execute:


{
  "query": "Why is our hiring process slow and where are candidates dropping off?",
  "scenario": "fix_slow_hiring",
  "filters": {},
  "max_agents": 5
}
The key changes:

"string" → actual question
"scenario": "string" → "fix_slow_hiring" (one of the 5 real scenario names)
"filters": {"additionalProp1": {}} → "filters": {} (empty is fine)
Valid scenario values:

"fix_slow_hiring"
"balance_workload"
"investigate_rejections"
"executive_metrics"
"interviewer_feedback"
