How do I save all teh Claude outputs in a md file
A few ways depending on what you need:

Option 1 — Claude Code built-in export (easiest)
In the Claude Code CLI, run:


/export
This saves the entire conversation (your messages + Claude's responses) as a markdown file in the current directory.

Option 2 — Copy from the VS Code extension
If you're using the VS Code extension (which you are):

Click the three-dot menu (⋯) at the top of the Claude panel
Select "Export conversation" or "Copy as markdown"
Paste into a new .md file
Option 3 — Read the raw conversation file (already exists)
Your conversation is already saved at:


C:\Users\thoma\.claude\projects\c--Thomas-IK-CapStone-Project\03fbbac7-8f48-4443-ad87-1f4cd9c53c75.jsonl
Convert it to markdown with this one-liner:


.\run.bat -c "
import json, sys
lines = open(r'C:\Users\thoma\.claude\projects\c--Thomas-IK-CapStone-Project\03fbbac7-8f48-4443-ad87-1f4cd9c53c75.jsonl').readlines()
with open('conversation_export.md', 'w', encoding='utf-8') as f:
    for line in lines:
        msg = json.loads(line)
        role = msg.get('role', '')
        content = msg.get('content', '')
        if isinstance(content, list):
            content = ' '.join(c.get('text','') for c in content if isinstance(c, dict))
        if role and content:
            f.write(f'## {role.upper()}\n\n{content}\n\n---\n\n')
print('Saved to conversation_export.md')
"
Option 4 — Save just Claude's responses going forward
Pipe future run.bat output to a file:


.\run.bat scripts\test_day11.py 2>&1 | Tee-Object -FilePath outputs.md -Append
Recommended: Use /export — it's one command and produces clean markdown.

/export
/export isn't available in this environment.

/export
